Feature: spa-link-attributes (RETROACTIVE — commit 07bb39d, logged after the
changelog/ convention was introduced in 478c817)
Target module: SPAEngine

- data-* boolean attributes ("cache", "addToHistory", "loadIntoNode") now treat
  "false"/"0" as false instead of Boolean(string), which was always true for
  non-empty values.
- saveState skips history.pushState when the link opted out via the addToHistory
  attribute (previously read but never enforced).
- Per-link flags reset to their defaults on every navigation so one link's
  attributes no longer leak into subsequent clicks.

Affected projects: any consumer of vUX-spaEngine.js using per-link data attribute
opt-outs — they now behave as documented.
